# Every text file is checked out with LF on every platform, as it is stored.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true, the default on GitHub's
# Windows runners) rewrites text files to CRLF, and every test that reads a
# committed file byte for byte — the MIT LICENSE, README statements, the
# workflow it parses, canonical golden encodings, vendored contract copies —
# fails there while the file itself is correct. Found by release run
# 36044864451 (NEW_247A1).
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell reads LF scripts; nothing here needs CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=lf

# Never touched.
*.png binary
*.tga binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.wad binary
*.bsp binary
*.pak binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
